@*
    The document itself.

    Two things here are load-bearing rather than boilerplate:

    * alvo.js is loaded in <head>, not at the end of <body>. It applies the stored theme before the
      first paint — a theme applied after paint is a flash, and under server-interactive rendering
      the first paint happens before hydration, so there is a real window to flash in.

    * The stylesheet and the script are named through AlvoAdminAssets rather than spelled here, so
      a rename is a compiler error instead of a blank page.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <base href="/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@AlvoAdminAssets.StyleSheet" />
    <script src="@AlvoAdminAssets.Script"></script>
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    <AdminRoutes />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
